## Remaining work and review notes

- Continue the source-to-target semantic read, then adjudicate the collected correction batch and complete the independent dependency-aware diff review under the universal editorial protocol. All 16,538 accepted IDs have draft text and passed the initial coverage/protected-value preflight; editorial acceptance is still pending.
- Resolved a contextual mistranslation of `Выдать явку в КЧС`: the Russian TV instruction says to issue the Visitor a requirement to report to KChS. `common-options-002.authored.json` now uses `Berikan perintah untuk menghadap KChS`; all 245 exact repetitions in `dialogue-batch-003.json` were regenerated, expansion verified, and the batch revalidated. Recheck this in the full semantic audit.
- An earlier run added 600 dialogue IDs in batches 075–092. All passed the structural validator. Source-bound corrections covered mushroom size, an indiscriminate shot, the two sisters’ age-neutral relationship, the miner’s rope signal, and preserving the digit `10` in an Alkonost line. Two intentionally garbled Foreigner strings in batch 083 remain exact. The Sirin/Alkonost scene was drafted from Russian with the glossary’s sister relationship and a formal `Anda` address for Alkonost. The poetic Death ending in batch 055 and surreal TV passage in batch 070 require special attention in the eventual complete semantic review. The whole-corpus sweep found no duplicate or unknown IDs and no extra exact-span classes beyond validated prefixes, placeholders and markup.
- The previous run added 224 dialogue IDs in batches 093–097: Alkonost, Rocker, and Luka. Each batch passed the structural validator, including Rocker’s `{0}` placeholder and the exact `Unstable:` speaker prefix. The Rocker retained music jargon and rough speech; Luka retained the distinction between his losses, guilt, and forgiveness. His source switches from a masculine to feminine pronoun in batch 097, so the Indonesian line explicitly corrects itself with `maksudku, perempuan itu`; verify this choice during the full semantic read.
- The previous run added 189 dialogue IDs in batches 098–104: Luka’s examination lines, Mother’s arrival/confession/examination, seven household lines, and Fairytaller’s arrival and stories. Every batch passed the structural validator. A source check corrected Mother’s sleepless duration to `sehari semalam`; Fairytaller’s story retained its folk-tale register and explicit `Kota Dingin`. Mother’s changing account of the missing children remains attributed to her.
- The previous run added 226 dialogue IDs in batches 105–111: Fairytaller examination, wheelchair-visitor variant scenes, and Foreigner narration/player choices. All passed structural validation. In batch 108, 19 Russian narration/choice lines were translated and 35 deliberately garbled utterances were preserved exactly; batch 109 preserved another 28 garbled utterances exactly. Batch 107 transliterated one Cyrillic phonetic utterance (`Выыыф. Ффыыыы.`) into Latin sound spelling; revisit that choice in the full semantic review. The wheelchair visitor’s standing and no-legs branches remain distinct.
